  <title>Receive orders</title>

  <p>The <gui>Receive Orders</gui> button of the main window counts in a
  shipment. A purchase order is listed here once the vendor's invoice for it
  has been entered in <link xref="unprocessed_po"/>, until all of it has
  arrived. <gui>Reload</gui> refreshes the list.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Purchase Order</gui>, and the location the
    products go to in the box beside <gui>Location</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select each line and set <gui>Received</gui> to how many arrived.
    Or click <gui>Receive all products</gui> if everything ordered
    came.</p></item>
    <item><p>For a product sold by serial number, type or scan each one into
    <gui>Serial numbers</gui> and press <key>Enter</key>. The count beside the
    list shows how many of the received ones are identified. <gui>Remove</gui>
    deletes a serial number entered by mistake, unless it has since been sold
    or has events recorded.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Close Purchase Order</gui>. It reads <gui>Post Partial
    Receipt</gui> when not everything has arrived.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Posting puts the received products in stock at the chosen location. A
  partly received order stays on the list, so the rest can be counted in when
  it comes. If some serial numbered products have no serial numbers entered,
  you are told which and asked whether to post anyway.</p>

  <p>Check <gui>Print labels when receiving</gui> to print a shelf label, with
  price, barcode and shelf location, for each product as it is counted in.
  The <gui>Location</gui> button opens <link xref="locations"/>. Right click a
  line for its <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p>

</page>
